kdp-workbooks/

# Session scratch: probe scripts, diagnostic dumps, and downloaded installers.
# The Docker Desktop installer here is 117MB and .tmp-docker/ is 93MB — GitHub
# hard-rejects any single file over 100MB, so committing these does not just
# bloat the repo, it makes `git push` fail outright.
.tmp-docker/
.tmp-*.exe
.tmp-*.txt
.tmp-*.html
.tmp-*.ps1
tmp-preview-diag*.txt
tmp-preview-diag*.json
tmp-parse-lovable-out*.txt
scripts/tmp-*.mjs

# Probe scripts written into the migration app during the port (any depth).
npm-install-result.txt
_gen_probe.mjs
_regen.mjs
_verify_routes.mjs

# Session scratch: one-shot push/cleanup scripts and their transcripts. These
# are generated per-task and hardcode a single commit message, so they are not
# reusable; they stay on disk for reference but must not enter the repo.
push-*.bat
push-*.ps1
push-*result.txt
phase3-*.ps1
# Generalised 2026-07-30. The list above was per-batch, so each new session added
# more untracked files: 40 of them were sitting in the root at once, and `git stash`
# during a merge then got entangled with them (the stash could not remove them, so
# `stash pop` refused with "already exists" and left a phantom stash entry).
#
# These patterns are PREFIX-based on purpose, so the next batch of one-shot scripts
# is covered without editing this file again. Anything matching is a script that
# hardcodes one commit message or one migration id - re-running it later would do
# the wrong thing, which is exactly why it must not look like repo tooling.
phase*.ps1
phase*result.txt
ship-*.ps1
ship-*.txt
finish.ps1
finish-result.txt
apply-1*.ps1
rollback-*.ps1
tidy.ps1
chk.ps1
r.bat
ping.txt
*-result.txt
*-console.txt

# Reusable dev helpers - these stay TRACKED and must not be caught above.
# (Negations are belt-and-braces: none of the patterns match them today, but they
# document the intent if someone broadens a pattern later.)
!setup-mobile.ps1
!start-dev.ps1
!run-dev.bat
!migrate.bat

# One-off capture dumps that were committed by mistake in merge e4fb9f9. The DOM
# dump alone is 388K of a third party's markup - reference material for cloning the
# editor layout, not source, and nothing in the app reads it.
tmp-lovable-*
__rmtest__.txt
phase3-*result.txt
remove-nextjs*.ps1
remove-result.txt
__sim.js
__sync_marker__.txt
__tsc-scope.json
